        992
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## B2B Distributor Order Anomaly Detector\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow runs on a schedule to pull pending B2B distributor orders from Google Sheets, enrich them with customer, order history, product, credit, and returns data, then builds a risk-analysis context. An AI agent using Gemini evaluates whether an order is anomalous or risky, and the workflow writes the decision back to the order record. If review is required, it creates a review record, alerts Sales in Slack, and logs the outcome for auditing.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure Google Sheets credentials with access to the workbook containing pending orders, customers, order history, products, credit, returns, review records, and audit log data.\n- Configure Slack credentials and set the target Slack channel ID in the Config node.\n- Configure Google Gemini credentials for the AI Agent chat model.\n- Update the Config node values for sheet_id, slack_channel_id, and currency.\n- Verify that the Google Sheets nodes point to the correct sheets, ranges, lookup keys, and update columns expected by the workflow.\n- Review the Schedule Trigger frequency to match how often pending orders should be checked.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the AI Agent prompt, structured output schema, and Prepare Decision fields to change risk criteria, anomaly labels, confidence thresholds, or escalation behavior.\n\n@[youtube](f7Kh1q_xL9I)"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
